<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37404" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praecinctus</span></b> ,
		ūs, m.
		praecingo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a girding.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (ante-class.): castula est palliolum
			praecinctui, Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 548,
			30</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in gen., <i>a
			dressing</i>, <i>dress</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in praecinctu ponens omnem decorem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 2, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
